//BUG="a comment line can silently move the statement below it into another block"
//OUT="done"

// The worst shape of the defect in 44 and 45, because nothing is reported.
// The comment sits at the end of the `if` body, indented 8. Its newline is
// swallowed (`Location::SingleLineComment` in src/compiler/preprocessor.rs),
// so its 8 spaces are glued in front of the 4 of the next line, and
// `out "done"` is read as indented 12: a block nested inside the `if` body.
//
// The program compiles, and prints nothing at all — `out "done"` now runs
// only when `x == 2`. The mirror image is just as quiet: a comment indented 4
// in front of a statement indented 4 that follows a loop pulls the statement
// into the loop body.
//
// Nothing about the source suggests any of this; the comment is where anyone
// would put it.

fn main
    x = 1
    if x == 2
        out "two "
        // nothing else to do for this case
    out "done"
